  <main>

    <section>
      <p><small>Screening mockups</small></p>
      <h1>Portfolio</h1>
      <p>These mockups show how HireLens screens resumes. Each example uses sample candidates and a sample job description.</p>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <section>
      <h2>Mockup 1: Ranked candidates</h2>
      <figure>
        <img src="images/mockup-ranking.png" alt="Ranked list of three candidates with scores" width="480" height="300">
        <figcaption>Candidates ranked against a Frontend Developer job description.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>The recruiter pastes a job description and uploads resumes. HireLens returns a ranked list, with the best match at the top.</p>
      <table border="1" cellpadding="6">
        <caption>Sample ranking for Frontend Developer</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Rank</th>
            <th scope="col">Candidate</th>
            <th scope="col">Score</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1</td><td>Candidate A</td><td>92</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2</td><td>Candidate B</td><td>81</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3</td><td>Candidate C</td><td>74</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <section>
      <h2>Mockup 2: Score breakdown</h2>
      <figure>
        <img src="images/mockup-breakdown.png" alt="Score breakdown showing matched and missing keywords" width="480" height="300">
        <figcaption>Matched and missing keywords for one candidate.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>Every score comes with a breakdown, so the recruiter can see why a candidate ranked where they did.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Matched:</strong> HTML, CSS, JavaScript</li>
        <li><strong>Missing:</strong> Git</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <section>
      <h2>Mockup 3: Blind review mode</h2>
      <figure>
        <img src="images/mockup-blind.png" alt="Candidate list with names and contact details hidden" width="480" height="300">
        <figcaption>Names and contact details hidden while ranking.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>Blind review hides personal details, so candidates are compared on skills and experience.</p>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <section>
      <h2>Mockups at a glance</h2>
      <table border="1" cellpadding="6">
        <caption>Summary of screening mockups</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Mockup</th>
            <th scope="col">What it shows</th>
            <th scope="col">Related service</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Ranked candidates</td>
            <td>A list ordered by score</td>
            <td>Candidate ranking</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Score breakdown</td>
            <td>Matched and missing keywords</td>
            <td>Explained scores</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Blind review mode</td>
            <td>Hidden names and contact details</td>
            <td>Blind review mode</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Read more about each feature on the <a href="services.html">Services</a> page, or see <a href="media.html">how scoring works</a>.</p>
    </section>

  </main>

